00:51:06.496 --> 00:51:09.430
A voice said quietly.

00:51:09.490 --> 00:51:12.291
It was Mr. Noel.

00:51:12.351 --> 00:51:17.403
She can tell us the truth about her mother.

00:51:17.463 --> 00:51:20.424
For a minute.

00:51:20.484 --> 00:51:23.676
My mother did not move.

00:51:23.736 --> 00:51:29.458
And she ran across the room and shouted at me.

00:51:29.518 --> 00:51:34.560
You know nothing, you bad child.

00:51:34.620 --> 00:51:37.153
And I'm your mother.

00:51:37.213 --> 00:51:39.846
Don't forget that.

00:51:39.906 --> 00:51:45.798
The guards ran after my mother and pulled her to the floor.

00:51:45.859 --> 00:51:48.860
I'm now which?

00:51:48.920 --> 00:51:50.820
My mother shouted.

00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:53.291
It's all lies.

00:51:53.351 --> 00:51:58.653
Janet, you're a witch, a child of the devil.

00:51:58.713 --> 00:52:04.815
You're my daughter, and I know.

00:52:04.875 --> 00:52:11.738
I was afraid, and I put my hands over my eyes.

00:52:11.798 --> 00:52:16.991
I didn't want to see my mother's ugly face.

00:52:17.051 --> 00:52:24.176
The guards pulled my mother out of the room, and the noise stopped.

00:52:24.236 --> 00:52:33.874
Janet, device, the judge said, tell us the truth about your mother.

00:52:33.934 --> 00:52:42.802
Roger Noel lifted me up and put me on a table in front of the judge.

00:52:42.862 --> 00:52:48.826
My mother is a witch, I began.

00:52:48.886 --> 00:52:54.338
She has a friend, a dog called Ball.

00:52:54.399 --> 00:53:00.042
When she wants to kill somebody, she tells Ball.

00:53:00.102 --> 00:53:04.184
I talked and talked.

00:53:04.244 --> 00:53:08.815
I told the judge everything.

00:53:08.875 --> 00:53:13.698
Judge Bromley listened carefully.

00:53:13.758 --> 00:53:18.300
My child, is this the truth?

00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:21.842
Yes, I answered.

00:53:21.902 --> 00:53:26.045
I'm telling you the truth.

00:53:26.105 --> 00:53:31.856
The guards brought my mother back into the room again.

00:53:31.916 --> 00:53:37.716
Her face looked tired, and her eyes were red.

00:53:37.776 --> 00:53:45.772
Elizabeth, device, your daughter told us about your dog, ball.

00:53:45.832 --> 00:53:51.296
Your son, too, told us about the clay pictures.

00:53:51.356 --> 00:53:56.119
We know everything.

00:53:56.179 --> 00:54:00.094
My mother said nothing.

00:54:00.154 --> 00:54:06.671
She didn't look at the judge and she didn't look at me.

00:54:06.731 --> 00:54:13.896
Next, the guards brought my brother James into the room.

00:54:13.956 --> 00:54:19.260
When I saw James, I wanted to cry.

00:54:19.320 --> 00:54:27.631
James was thin and dirty and his hair was very long.

00:54:27.691 --> 00:54:35.098
He looked at the judge, and at all the rich and important men in the room.

00:54:35.158 --> 00:54:38.199
And he began to cry.

00:54:38.259 --> 00:54:42.030
Then he sat down on the floor.

00:54:42.090 --> 00:54:47.991
Stand up, James' device, Judge Bromley said.

00:54:48.051 --> 00:54:54.352
The guards pulled James up, but he fell to the floor again.

00:54:54.413 --> 00:54:57.892
You killed Mr. Duckworth.

00:54:57.953 --> 00:55:03.876
Judge Bromley said, I wanted a shirt.

00:55:03.936 --> 00:55:06.707
James cried.

00:55:06.767 --> 00:55:10.059
Is your brother a witch?

00:55:10.119 --> 00:55:13.201
Judge Bromley asked me.

00:55:13.261 --> 00:55:22.787
Yes, I said, my brother sat on the floor, his mouth open.

00:55:22.847 --> 00:55:28.844
He looked at me, but he didn't know me.

00:55:28.904 --> 00:55:35.418
I was clean and fat because of all the good food at Reed Hall.

00:55:35.478 --> 00:55:40.509
James told me about his friend Dandy.

00:55:40.570 --> 00:55:42.170
I began.

00:55:42.230 --> 00:55:49.422
Dandy was the devil and James heard the name Dandy, and he began to cry again.

00:55:49.442 --> 00:55:52.462
I want Dandy!

00:55:52.482 --> 00:55:56.075
I want to go home!

00:55:56.135 --> 00:56:02.498
The guards pulled him up from the floor and took him out of the room.

00:56:02.558 --> 00:56:07.318
I never saw my brother again.

00:56:07.378 --> 00:56:16.850
When the guards brought my sister Alison in front of the judge, I said nothing.

00:56:16.910 --> 00:56:22.782
John Law, the peddler, came into the room.

00:56:22.842 --> 00:56:25.906
He was a thin man now.

00:56:25.966 --> 00:56:34.824
he walked slowly, and he talked slowly, and his face looked ill.

00:56:34.884 --> 00:56:43.408
He told the judge about that day near cold, when Alison cursed him, and her dog ran after him.

00:56:43.428 --> 00:56:48.160
"'I'm sorry,' Alison said.

00:56:48.221 --> 00:57:05.983
I was angry with you that day, but I'm sorry now,' Alison's eyes were dark and afraid, but she had no friends in that room, and nobody wanted to listen to her.

00:57:06.043 --> 00:57:14.819
Then Mr. Knoll took me out, and I waited with his servant in a different room.

00:57:14.879 --> 00:57:25.400
An hour later, there was the noise of many people shouting and crying The servant smiled.

00:57:25.460 --> 00:57:28.224
The trial is finished.

00:57:28.284 --> 00:57:32.438
He said, You're a good child, Janet.

00:57:32.498 --> 00:57:36.974
You told the judge the truth about the witches.

00:57:37.034 --> 00:57:42.402
Mr. Noel took me home to read hall.

00:57:42.462 --> 00:58:02.524
and on the 20th day of August, 1612, the guards took my mother, my sister, and my brother out of prison and hanged them in front of Lancaster Castle.

00:58:02.584 --> 00:58:10.076
And so I lost my family.

00:58:10.136 --> 00:58:17.099
When I was a child, I wanted to be happy.

00:58:17.159 --> 00:58:24.706
I wanted to be warm, to wear shoes, to eat good food.

00:58:24.766 --> 00:58:28.838
I wanted someone to take care of me.

00:58:28.899 --> 00:58:30.990
That's all.

00:58:31.051 --> 00:58:34.073
My mother gave me nothing.

00:58:34.133 --> 00:58:36.926
She gave me no love.

00:58:36.986 --> 00:58:40.032
She never took care of me.

00:58:40.092 --> 00:58:49.572
Because my mother was a witch, my father ran away, and I never knew him.

00:58:49.632 --> 00:59:01.650
My father was a rich man without a name, and I lived hungry and cold with a witch.

00:59:01.710 --> 00:59:08.145
And so I told Judge Bromley the truth about my family.

00:59:08.205 --> 00:59:11.120
Was I wrong?

00:59:11.180 --> 00:59:14.596
I don't know.

00:59:14.656 --> 00:59:19.388
I was happy for years at Reed Hall.

00:59:19.448 --> 00:59:24.242
For 21 years, I forgot my family.

00:59:24.302 --> 00:59:27.804
I learnt to cook for the Noel family.

00:59:27.864 --> 00:59:35.398
I worked many hours every day, but I was warm and I ate good food.

00:59:35.458 --> 00:59:41.902
Every Sunday, in my best dress, I went to church.

00:59:41.962 --> 00:59:47.346
Every summer, I walked over Pendle Hill.

00:59:47.406 --> 00:59:55.489
I never thought about my family because I was happy at Reed Hall.

00:59:55.550 --> 01:00:05.604
In August, 1612, the guards hanged my family in front of Lancaster Castle.

01:00:05.664 --> 01:00:11.609
But their dead faces waited for me there.

01:00:11.669 --> 01:00:25.922
and a year ago, in 1633, when the guards put me in the prison in Lancaster Castle, I met them again.

01:00:25.982 --> 01:00:38.332
Day after day, I see their ugly, dead faces and hear their cold, angry voices.

01:00:38.392 --> 01:00:43.557
I think of them all the time.

01:00:43.617 --> 01:00:47.780
God is with me here, in prison.

01:00:47.840 --> 01:00:50.111
I believe that.

01:00:50.171 --> 01:00:55.523
But my dead family is with me too.

01:00:55.583 --> 01:01:03.406
Mr. Webster, from the church at Kildwick, visits me again.

01:01:03.466 --> 01:01:10.028
His blue eyes are tired, but he smiles at me.

01:01:10.088 --> 01:01:16.950
Edmund Robinson and his father told the truth in London.

01:01:17.010 --> 01:01:25.662
He says quietly, the child told lies about you because he was afraid of his father.

01:01:25.722 --> 01:01:30.044
He wanted his father to love him.

01:01:30.104 --> 01:01:33.745
I say nothing.

01:01:33.805 --> 01:01:40.710
Mr Webster wants to be kind, but he cannot help me.

01:01:40.770 --> 01:01:46.894
Mr. Noel cannot help me, because he is dead.

01:01:46.954 --> 01:01:51.326
Edmund Robinson is only a child.

01:01:51.386 --> 01:01:57.028
He tells lies one day, and the truth the next day.

01:01:57.088 --> 01:02:01.040
But the truth cannot help me.

01:02:01.100 --> 01:02:07.516
What can I do against hate and lies?

01:02:07.576 --> 01:02:14.664
When Mr. Noel was alive, the villagers didn't talk about me.

01:02:14.724 --> 01:02:19.447
But when Mr. Noel died, the lies began.

01:02:19.467 --> 01:02:27.744
The villagers are all afraid of me because my name is device.

01:02:27.804 --> 01:02:33.848
They hate me because my name is device.

01:02:33.908 --> 01:02:37.880
They say, I am a witch.

01:02:37.940 --> 01:02:42.082
because my name is device.

01:02:42.142 --> 01:02:50.026
I come from a family of witches, but I am not a witch.

01:02:50.086 --> 01:02:54.157
Nobody died because I cursed them.

01:02:54.217 --> 01:02:57.768
I never made clay pictures.

01:02:57.828 --> 01:03:02.220
I never had a cat or dog.

01:03:02.280 --> 01:03:07.958
I only wanted to live quietly at Reed Hall.

01:03:08.018 --> 01:03:13.926
and watch the changing skies over Pendle Hill.

01:03:13.986 --> 01:03:26.116
When I was a child, I was always cold and hungry, and I hated my family because they were witches.

01:03:26.176 --> 01:03:35.887
In 1612, I told the truth, and the truth killed my family.

01:03:35.947 --> 01:03:53.955
Twenty-two years later, lies are going to kill me, here in Lancaster Castle, and I am cold and hungry again.

01:03:54.015 --> 01:04:01.090
Mr. Webster gives me bread, and I go back into the prison.

01:04:01.150 --> 01:04:04.692
I can never go back to Reed Hall.

01:04:04.752 --> 01:04:07.296
I know that now.

01:04:07.356 --> 01:04:14.944
I must stay here in Lancaster Castle with my dead family.

01:04:15.004 --> 01:04:20.598
They are watching me and waiting for me.

01:04:20.658 --> 01:04:24.181
I can never be free of them.

01:04:24.241 --> 01:04:31.537
This is my true story and I want to finish it now.

